> Safe machine-word boundaries, explicit budgets and failure controls

The old code used one uint64_t for each parity row and each selection row.
A base of 64 primes permits 65 collected rows, making the identity shift
by 64 undefined. A compiled unchanged-source probe catches that shift;
another catches division by zero for modulus zero. The canonical kernel
now stores dynamically sized packed words and validates inputs before
allocation. Its supported base count is 1…4096 and modulus is at least two.
Exact widened modular products handle the full uint64_t range; the integer
square root uses exact comparisons, including values next to 2⁶⁴.

A zero candidate budget means no search and returns factor zero. Zero
residues are excluded before division; they are counted, never divided
repeatedly. Prime moduli can generate smooth relations and dependencies,
but no proper factor. Failure is also possible for composite inputs under
an insufficient budget or a batch of unhelpful congruences.

Owned capture has a default one-million scalar-cell cap. A collection
counts k base cells and k+3 cells per accepted relation (x,residue,offset,
and k exponents). A tested dependency adds its selected-index count,
k full exponent sums and four arithmetic values. The cap is checked before
each affected capture. Zero disables only this optional cap; domain,
endpoint, count and container limits remain. It excludes vector objects
and scratch elimination storage; it is not a byte quota. The compact
factor function retains no dependency history and has no optional cap.
The following executable shows exact versus one-short capture limits,
prime and zero-budget failure, and row counts crossing both 64 and 128.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dixon_limits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::dixon_factor_trace(77,3,10);
  const auto exact=dm::algorithms::dixon_factor_trace(77,3,10,t.captured_cells);
  std::size_t rejected=0;
  try {(void)dm::algorithms::dixon_factor_trace(77,3,10,t.captured_cells-1);}
  catch(const std::length_error&) {++rejected;}
  try {(void)dm::algorithms::dixon_factor(0,3);}
  catch(const std::invalid_argument&) {++rejected;}
  try {(void)dm::algorithms::dixon_collect(77,0,0);}
  catch(const std::invalid_argument&) {++rejected;}
  std::print("Exact cap {} cells returns {}; expected rejections {}.\n",t.captured_cells,exact.factor,rejected);
  const auto prime=dm::algorithms::dixon_factor_trace(13,3,20);
  const auto zero=dm::algorithms::dixon_factor_trace(77,3,0);
  const auto empty=dm::algorithms::dixon_collect(4,3,20);
  const auto wide=dm::algorithms::dixon_collect(std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max(),3,0);
  std::print("Prime 13: factor {}, tested dependencies {}. Composite 77 with zero budget: factor {}.\n",prime.factor,prime.dependencies.size(),zero.factor);
  std::print("Modulus 4: {} zero residues in {} candidates. Full-width modulus start {}.\n",empty.zero_residues,empty.scanned,wide.start);
  std::vector<double> x,rows,rank;
  std::print("\n| base size | collected rows | rank | nullity | returned factor |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int k:{3,30,63,64,65,96,127,128,129}) {
    const auto a=dm::algorithms::dixon_factor_trace(77,k,400);
    if(a.collection.relations.size()!=static_cast<std::size_t>(k+1)) throw std::runtime_error("incomplete control batch");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k,a.collection.relations.size(),a.rank,a.collection.relations.size()-a.rank,a.factor);
    x.push_back(k); rows.push_back(a.collection.relations.size()); rank.push_back(a.rank);
  }
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.line(x,rows,"rows",{37,99,235}).points(x,rows,"",{37,99,235},5)
   .line(x,rank,"rank",{220,38,38}).points(x,rank,"",{220,38,38},5)
   .title("Dynamic rows cross 64 and 128; rank stays data-dependent")
   .x_label("base size for modulus 77").y_label("collected rows and parity rank")
   .y_limits(-2,165).size(1100,570).save_svg("build/dixon_limits.svg");
}
```
